@ifnottex
@node Top
@top HeroicLands Emacs

Everything this configuration adds, in one place: working across the
sixteen repositories, editing TypeScript, and authoring content notes —
previewing the tables a note declares, querying the content index, and
writing wikilinks that are correct before the build ever sees them.

This package is its own repository, so it can be shared and so no single
machine holds the only copy.  Your own @file{init.el} adds it to
@code{load-path} and turns on @code{global-heroiclands-mode}; see
@ref{The Mode}.

Almost everything hangs off the @kbd{C-c h} prefix.  Press @kbd{C-c h}
and wait half a second; which-key lists what is there.  Every command
below documents itself in @kbd{C-h f}, and this manual is @kbd{C-c h ?}.

